From: Haldexx
Subject: [PATCH] input: show the hover spot under a hovering stylus

The S Pen's hover reaches apps and PointerChoreographer creates a stylus pointer
controller, but the default stylus icon is TYPE_NULL, so nothing is drawn unless
the app under the pen sets an icon. Use TYPE_SPOT_HOVER as the default.

---
diff --git a/services/core/jni/com_android_server_input_InputManagerService.cpp b/services/core/jni/com_android_server_input_InputManagerService.cpp
--- a/services/core/jni/com_android_server_input_InputManagerService.cpp
+++ b/services/core/jni/com_android_server_input_InputManagerService.cpp
@@ -2156,8 +2156,9 @@
 }
 
 PointerIconStyle NativeInputManager::getDefaultStylusIconId() {
-    // Use the empty icon as the default pointer icon for a hovering stylus.
-    return PointerIconStyle::TYPE_NULL;
+    // Show the hover spot under a hovering stylus.
+    // An app that sets its own stylus pointer icon still overrides this default.
+    return PointerIconStyle::TYPE_SPOT_HOVER;
 }
 
 PointerIconStyle NativeInputManager::getCustomPointerIconId() {
